; farglass - the SELinux policy module of farglass (F081)
;
; farglassctl loads this file with: semodule -X 200 -i farglass.cil
;
; The session worker of farglass-login runs in the domain unconfined_service_t.
; pam_selinux sets the context of the user for the agent, usually unconfined_t.
; The default policy of RHEL and Fedora refuses that domain transition, and the
; agent does not start. This rule permits it.
;
; The rule applies to each program in unconfined_service_t, not only to farglass.
; A policy without these types ignores the optional block.
(optional farglass_session
    (allow unconfined_service_t unconfined_t (process (transition)))
)
